# Contracts Integration

RULE: UAC for external APIs (Databento, CCXT, Tardis). UIC for internal schemas (pubsub, lifecycle, features, ML, risk, events). Never `unified_api_contracts.internal`. Raw venue responses → UAC normalizers → canonical types before returning.
WHY: Type safety, VCR mocks, canonical format; internal SSOT is UIC.
CODEX: 02-data/contracts-scope-and-layout.md, 05-infrastructure/contracts-integration.md

Typed response models: Adapters MUST use Pydantic `model_validate()` at API boundary; never `dict[str, Any]`. See no-type-any-use-specific.mdc.
Domain schemas: UIC `domain/<service-name>/`; services never define locally. SchemaDefinition stays in service.
Adapter models: `_<venue>_models.py` → UAC `unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/schemas.py`; private prefix does not exempt.

NEVER: from unified_api_contracts.internal; dict[str, Any] for API responses; raw venue responses to services; domain contracts in service repos; adapter models in interface repos
